audit='''<p class="eyebrow">Demonstration readiness</p><h1>The tools must demonstrate the rules</h1><p class="lead">The current offline PySide assistants now emphasize the next available action, maintain explicit state and support a task-based focus order. Broader host and production validation remains separate and visible.</p><div class="status"><strong>Completed:</strong> existing 87-test suite passed after the code changes. Nine matching sample states were rendered before and after. Starting, preview, completion and narrow warning states were visually inspected. Actual offscreen Tab events followed parent material → name → slot → review → Preview → Reset → task tabs, skipping disabled Apply. Measured primary and secondary action text pairs are 10.17:1 and 9.64:1 respectively. These are offline checks and selected color pairs, not proof of live Unreal integration or complete accessibility.</div><h2>Concrete changes</h2><ul><li>Preview receives primary emphasis before a plan exists; Apply receives it when the reviewed plan is ready.</li><li>Warning acknowledgment and blocked states retain their guards. After completion, the result remains visible without encouraging an immediate repeated Apply.</li><li>Action colors now have a small shared token source. Existing canvas colors remain in the legacy shared style; full token migration is not claimed.</li><li>Keyboard order is explicitly set to follow the task; review surfaces receive visible focus styling.</li><li>The style sheet records roles, states, layout rules, validation and the AI maintenance workflow.</li></ul>'''
