diag='''<p class="eyebrow">A repeatable visual critique</p><h1>Look at the same tool three ways</h1><p class="lead">Keep the task in mind: review the material assignment, then apply it. Each diagnostic asks a different question.</p><div class="diagnostic-controls" role="group" aria-label="Visual diagnostic"><button data-mode="normal" aria-pressed="true">Original</button><button data-mode="gray" aria-pressed="false">Grayscale</button><button data-mode="squint" aria-pressed="false">Squint approximation</button><button data-mode="shapes" aria-pressed="false">Layout blockout</button></div><p id="diagnostic-caption" aria-live="polite">Original current practice capture. Read the labels and inspect the task.</p><div class="diagnostic-frame"><img id="diagnostic-image" src="after/material_preview.png" alt="Actual material preview in the offline PySide assistant"><div id="shape-view" class="shape-view" role="img" aria-label="Simplified schematic of the same material tool layout"><div class="sh-title"></div><div class="sh-inputs"></div><div class="sh-status"></div><div class="sh-review"></div><div class="sh-primary"></div><div class="sh-secondary"></div><div class="sh-reset"></div></div></div><p class="meta">Grayscale and blur are browser display filters on an actual screenshot. The blockout is an editable CSS schematic, not a captured or implemented UI.</p><div class="grid"><section class="tile"><h3>What survives?</h3><p>In grayscale, inspect light/dark hierarchy without hue. While squinting—or using the coarse blur approximation—inspect the large masses of emphasis. In the blockout, inspect grouping, proportion, alignment and flow without wording.</p></section><section class="tile"><h3>What remains untested?</h3><p>These checks do not establish measured text contrast, color-vision accessibility, keyboard access, comprehension or successful task completion. Return to the original, use actual controls, and observe an attempt.</p></section></div><p>Art value is perceived lightness/darkness. HSV Value is a model coordinate; it is not the same quantity as WCAG relative luminance. Equal HSV values do not guarantee equal readability.</p>'''
diagscript='''<script>const descriptions={normal:'Original current practice capture. Read the labels and inspect the task.',gray:'Grayscale: does priority remain readable without hue? This is not a color-vision simulation.',squint:'Squint approximation: where does the largest visual emphasis remain? Blur is a coarse proxy, not a readability test.',shapes:'Simplified layout blockout: inspect grouping and proportion. This schematic intentionally omits detail.'};for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('[data-mode]'))b.addEventListener('click',()=>{const mode=b.dataset.mode;for(const x of document.querySelectorAll('[data-mode]'))x.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(x===b));document.querySelector('#diagnostic-caption').textContent=descriptions[mode];const im=document.querySelector('#diagnostic-image');im.style.display=mode==='shapes'?'none':'block';im.style.filter=mode==='gray'?'grayscale(1)':mode==='squint'?'blur(5px)':'none';document.querySelector('#shape-view').style.display=mode==='shapes'?'block':'none';});</script>'''
write('diagnostics.html','Visual checks on the current tool',diag,diagscript)

